# OCI images pre-warmed into the `deployer-installed` snapshot by step2b, so a
# `livetest --all` run does NOT trigger ~4 concurrent skopeo extractions on the
# 4-core/8GB nested VM (that resource spike is what made deploys blow past the
# 600s CLI timeout — see memory: livetest-mass-break-is-environmental).
#
# Each line is an `oci_image` ref fed to host-get-oci-image.py (same code path
# as a real deploy → identical vztmpl tarball name → guaranteed cache hit).
# One `#`-comment or blank line is ignored.
#
# ONE image is deliberately left OUT so the skopeo download+extract branch keeps
# getting exercised by a real scenario: **eclipse-mosquitto** (smallest image at
# ~10 MB, simplest scenario with no deps). NOTE: ghcr.io/proxvex/proxvex can NOT
# serve this purpose — build-proxvex-oci-image.sh always aliases the locally-built
# deployer into the cache as proxvex_latest.tar / proxvex_<ver>.tar (so tests use
# the build under test), so proxvex/* always cache-hit regardless of this list.
#
# Regenerate tags after image bumps from a warm run:
#   ssh -p 1222 root@ubuntupve 'ls /var/lib/vz/template/cache/*.tar'
# and map <name>_<tag>.tar back to the app's oci_image base.
ghcr.io/proxvex/debian-docker:latest
distribution/distribution:3.1.1
ghcr.io/esphome/esphome:2026.7.2
gitea/gitea:1.26.4
misterbabou/gptwol:7.1.5
homebridge/homebridge:2026-07-20
ghcr.io/modbus2mqtt/modbus2mqtt:0.32.1
nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1-alpine
nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.31.3
nginx:alpine
nodered/node-red:5.0.1
dpage/pgadmin4:9.16
ghcr.io/proxvex/playwright:v1.57.0-noble
postgres:16-alpine
ghcr.io/proxvex/wolproxy:latest
ghcr.io/koenkk/zigbee2mqtt:2.12.1
